    "body": "2026 Paris Motor Show • The Volkswagen Group's Affordable BEV Quartet Has Almost Reached 150,000 Orders\n2028 Bentley Supersports Convertible Spied With Coupe Brother's Aerodynamic Upgrades\n53 photos\nPhoto: SH Proshots\nFollowing the introduction of the Supersports coupe for model year 2027, the go-faster Continental story will continue in 2027 with a convertible. Likely scheduled for production as a 2028 model, the open-top derivative was caught at the Nurburgring with little in the way of camouflage.\nDressed in matte black and carrying similar aerodynamic updates, the Supersports Convertible is anything but a Continental GTC with a bad attitude. Starting from its rear end, a very telling decklid spoiler is joined by a serious-looking aerodynamic diffuser. Being a V8, it should come as no surprise that four exhaust outlets are on the menu.\nFrom the rear end alone, there is little attempt to soften the high-performance treatment for someone who merely wants to enjoy open-top driving. Its matte-finish body panels are complemented by Pirelli-fied black wheels, keeping the prototype's look consistent. Sill extensions and purposeful side bumper sculpting also indicate how different the Supersports is from the Continental.\nAs far as width is concerned, the coupe had its rear track widened by 16 millimeters (0.6 inches) because the Supersports drops all-wheel drive and plug-in hybrid nonsense for a purer drivetrain. The rear-drive special edition also benefits from rear-wheel steering and an electronically controlled limited-slip rear differential, a recipe that carries over to the convertible.\nA distinctive grille, bumper, and a quarter of dive planes dominate the front end. Those small blades at the sides of the front bumper are designed to reduce front lift, whereas the outer front bumper intakes satisfy engine and brake cooling requirements. Compared to the far more discreet Continental GTC, that's a whole lot of front-end furniture.\nPhoto: Baldauf While it's not clear if Bentley can mirror the coupe's downforce levels, stability at speed is the name of the game here. Carrying more than a token lip beneath its nose, the prototype also prides itself on carbon-ceramic brakes. Don't expect anything other than a familiar V8 underhood, namely the 4.0-liter unit we already know from the Conti.\nIn this gasoline-only application, it produces a devilish 666 metric horsepower and 800 Newton-meters of twist. Make that 657 mechanical ponies and 590 pound-feet on the right octane, with most of that fury channeled to the rear axle by a dual-clutch tranny.\nBreathing out through an Akrapovic lightweight exhaust system, the Supersports coupe weighs 1,998 kilograms (4,405 pounds) in European flavor. Bentley achieved this by deleting a lot of stuff, creating a more purist driving experience in the process. With the convertible's roof arrangement, matching that figure would be a substantial undertaking.\nBe it similar in weight or heavier, the Supersports Convertible will undoubtedly hit 100 kph (62 mph) in less than four seconds when equipped with the stickiest of tires. Maximum speed? As long as the roof is up, expect no more than 320 kilometers per hour (199 miles per hour).\nWith the coupe's 500-unit production run already spoken for, it's only a matter of time until the convertible goes live. Given the mostly nonexistent camouflage, fingers crossed Bentley will debut next month at the 2026 Los Angeles Auto Show.\nLiked the article? Follow us to see more articles from autoevolution in your Google feeds.\nBentley Supersports Convertible 2028 Bentley Supersports Convertible Bentley spyshots design spy shots Nurburgring\nAbout the author: Mircea Panait\nAfter a 1:43 scale model of a Ferrari 250 GTO sparked Mircea's interest for cars when he was a kid, an early internship at Top Gear sealed his career path. He's most interested in muscle cars and American trucks, but he takes a passing interest in quirky kei cars as well. Full profile\nUP NEXT Acura's Road to 200,000 Yearly Sales in the US Includes RDX Hybrid and Two Larger SUVs",
